{"term":"amaze","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c2699a65d9bd9404b2","definition":"To fill (someone) with surprise and wonder; to astonish, to astound, to surprise.","example":"He was amazed when he found that the girl was a robot.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amaze","astonish","astound","bewitch","surprise","wow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:efb30f7bf143650955","definition":"To stun or stupefy (someone).","example":"Inſtead of thinking hovv to remedy this diſorder by rallying ſuch troops as fled, or by oppoſing freſh troops to ſtop the progreſs of the conquerors, being totally amazed by this firſt blovv, he [Pompey] returned to the camp, and in his tent, vvaited the iſſue of an event, vvhich it vvas his duty to direct, not to follovv: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amaze","astonish","astound","bewitch","surprise","wow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:388efe321401003d2f","definition":"To bewilder or perplex (someone or oneself).","example":"The many musits thought the which he goes / Are like a labyrinth to amaze his foes.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amaze","astonish","astound","bewitch","surprise","wow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, obsolete, reflexive","register":"also, obsolete, reflexive, transitive","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a4ff552a1e7e1e056d","definition":"To fill (someone) with panic; to panic, to terrify.","example":"It [fear] amaſeth many men that are to ſpeake, or ſhevv themſelues in publike aſſemblies, or before ſome great personages, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amaze","astonish","astound","bewitch","surprise","wow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, poetic","register":"obsolete, poetic, transitive","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5991d1cd1170786ee8","definition":"To experience amazement; to be astounded.","example":"Madam amaze not, ſee his Maieſtie / Returnd vvith glory from the holy land.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amaze","astonish","astound","bewitch","surprise","wow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, intransitive","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6517edc7f0b511962c","definition":"Amazement, astonishment; (countable) an instance of this.","example":"All in amaze he ſuddenly vp ſtart / VVith ſvvord in hand, and vvith the old man vvent; […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, uncountable","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly","amazeful"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a0f15bc5301c39316","definition":"Fear, terror.","example":"[T]he whole rout was in amaze; his Lordſhip turned all manner of colours, my Lady fell into a ſwoon; […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["amazement"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, uncountable","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly","amazeful"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea0bf8ed8f4e1e4350","definition":"Stupefaction of the mind; bewilderment; (countable) an instance of this.","example":"[T]he panicles or thin skins [of a horse] vvhich cleauing to the bones, doe couer the vvhole braine, are ſubiect to headache, mygram [migrane], dizineſſe, and amazes; […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["amazement"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly","amazeful"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:11c63fdcf48fb7d3f8","definition":"Clipping of amazing.","example":"As incredibly amaze the aftermath in FFoD was, it would have been nice to see the post-Unicron battle for Cybertron.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["amazeballs"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, clipping, slang","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, clipping, slang","wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly","amazeful"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/əˈmeɪz/"},"wordFamily":["amazeballs","amazed","amazedly","amazedness","amazement","amazing","amazingly","amazingness","unamazed","unamazedly","amazeful"]}